Native-wide polygon test: draw what the revealed margins show.

Crash 2's renderers drop a polygon when every projected vertex lies past the
same edge of the 512x217 screen, a packed test on the GTE's SXY words
(B = 0x00D90200 = 217<<16 | 512):

    t8 = ~((s0-B) | (s1-B) | (s2-B)) | (s0 & s1 & s2)
    bltz t8, reject    ; all Y past the top or bottom
    sll  t8, t8, 16
    bltz t8, reject    ; all X < 0, or all X >= 512

Squash widescreen (mode 1) squeezes X in the GTE before this test, so the game
tests the wider view. Native-wide (mode 2) leaves the GTE alone and draws the
extra columns through the GPU draw offset, so the game still tested [0,512):
every polygon wholly inside a revealed margin was dropped and only polygons
straddling the old 4:3 edge reached it - the broken edges native-wide showed.
Patch 0046 (objects) and 0016 (the object box cull) could not touch this. The
level draw lists already hold these polygons (NOTES, widescreen part 4).

Seven sites use the test: model triangles (0x80041C18), world triangles and
quads in both loops of func_80041E5C (0x800424E0, 0x800427A0, 0x80045EC4,
0x800460D0), lines (0x8004518C) and 1x1 dots, right edge only (0x80045404).
Every branch in the generated code calls psx_check_interrupts_at with the PC it
continues at, and nothing else enters these blocks, so the X-branch block is
reached only after the Y branch fell through, with t8 = mask<<16.

crash2_wide_reject.h (new) re-decides X there against [-off, 512+off), the
window native-wide shows, and clears bit 31 of t8 when the polygon reaches into
it. It only turns rejects into keeps, and only for polygons squash mode already
draws at the same aspect, so primitive-buffer use is what squash produces. t8
is scratch on every kept path. Quads project their fourth vertex between the
reads and the test; both store vertex 0 at [v1+376] first, which is where it is
read. Before changing anything the hook recomputes the game's own verdict from
the vertices it read and leaves the polygon alone if they disagree. Identity at
4:3, in squash mode and on frames presented 4:3. 141 code words are checked
(once, and again after a state load).

PSX_CRASH2_WIDE_REJECT=0 turns it off; the c2_reject debug command switches it
live and reports counters, carried by the heartbeat as "wide_reject". Checked
against the real instructions of all seven sites run through a MIPS
interpreter (tuning/wide_reject_sim): no change at margin 0, the game's verdict
reproduced exactly, the widened verdict at 14:9 and 16:9, no other state
touched, and the code-word guard.

No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake; overlay shards are unaffected.

